{% doc %}
  Presentation shell for the `maps` block.

  Renders `<maps-component>` → the card (dropdown + the captured branch panels) and the deferred map
  slot. All capturing/splitting of the child blocks stays in `blocks/maps.liquid`; this
  snippet only lays the two halves out. The map itself is NEVER server-rendered — `<maps-component>`
  injects the Embed API iframe once the block enters the viewport.

  @param {object} settings - The parent block settings.
  @param {string} [options_html] - Captured `<option>` fragments from the `_maps-location` children.
  @param {string} [panels_html] - Captured info-panel fragments from the same children.
  @param {number} [item_count] - How many branches were captured (0 → editor onboarding).
  @param {boolean} [render_card] - Whether the card renders at all (`show_card` on AND ≥ 1 branch).
  @param {string} [fallback_query] - Pre-escaped map query for when there is no `<select>` to read.
  @param {string} [fallback_title] - Pre-escaped iframe title to go with `fallback_query`.
  @param {string} [block_id] - The parent block's id — makes the `<select>` id unique per instance.
  @param {string} [color_scheme] - Color scheme suffix (blank when inheriting).
  @param {string} [block_style] - Inline spacing / size / border / gap / map CSS vars for the root.
  @param {string} [shopify_attributes] - Theme editor attributes for the outer root.

  @example
  {% render 'maps-markup', settings: block.settings, options_html: options_html, panels_html: panels_html, item_count: 2 %}
{% enddoc %}
{{ 'scoped-maps.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign item_count = item_count | default: 0
  assign render_card = render_card | default: false, allow_false: true
  assign layout_mobile = settings.layout_mobile | default: 'stacked'

  comment
    The Theme Editor onboarding hint. It used to live inside the card, but at 0 locations there IS no
    card any more (the map renders standalone instead), so it is its own element alongside the map —
    the merchant still has to be told where locations come from.
  endcomment
  assign show_onboarding = false
  if item_count == 0 and request.design_mode
    assign show_onboarding = true
  endif

  assign position = settings.card_position | default: 'top-right' | split: '-'
  assign position_block = position[0] | default: 'top'
  assign position_inline = position[1] | default: 'right'

  assign has_api_key = false
  if settings.api_key != blank
    assign has_api_key = true
  endif

  comment
    NO `gap-style` on the root, and none on `.maps__card-inner` either: both of those gaps are
    literals from the Spacing table (card→map 24 on stacked mobile, dropdown→panel 20/24) and must
    stay independent of `card_gap` / `card_gap_mobile`. Since round 3 those two settings mean the
    rhythm BETWEEN the blocks a merchant nests inside a location, so their only consumer is
    `.maps__panel` (which carries `gap-style`); the `--f-row-gap*` vars emit on the root and inherit
    down to it.
  endcomment
  assign root_class = 'maps spacing-style size-style'
  assign root_class = root_class | append: ' maps--mobile-' | append: layout_mobile
  assign root_class = root_class | append: ' maps--v-' | append: position_block
  assign root_class = root_class | append: ' maps--h-' | append: position_inline
  if item_count == 1
    comment
      Exactly one branch (the shipped default) — a <select> with a single option is dead UI, so the
      dropdown is hidden. The <option> stays in the DOM: it carries the branch's map query for the JS.

      `== 1`, not `< 2`: with ZERO branches there is no card and no <select> at all, so calling that
      state "single" would be a class that lies about the DOM it is on.
    endcomment
    assign root_class = root_class | append: ' maps--single'
  endif
  if color_scheme != blank
    assign root_class = root_class | append: ' color-' | append: color_scheme
  endif

  comment
    The card's OWN padding, deliberately separate from the block's `padding-*` group — TWO AXES, not
    four sides: one setting and one var per axis, per device, feeding `padding-block` /
    `padding-inline` directly. A 4-side control was finer than both the design and the CSS under it.
    Flat px per device rather than a `clamp()` ramp: the design is a literal 24 at every desktop
    width, and a ramp up from mobile 0 would leave the card at ~0 padding at 768px, exactly where the
    map floor is at its shortest too.
  endcomment
  capture card_style
    echo '--maps-card-padding-block: '
    echo settings['card-padding-block'] | default: 0
    echo 'px;--maps-card-padding-inline: '
    echo settings['card-padding-inline'] | default: 0
    echo 'px;--maps-card-padding-block-mobile: '
    echo settings['card-padding-block-mobile'] | default: 0
    echo 'px;--maps-card-padding-inline-mobile: '
    echo settings['card-padding-inline-mobile'] | default: 0
    echo 'px;'
  endcapture
  assign card_style = card_style | strip | strip_newlines
-%}

<maps-component
  class="{{ root_class }}"
  style="{{ block_style | strip | strip_newlines }}"
  data-api-key="{{ settings.api_key | escape }}"
  data-zoom="{{ settings.zoom | default: 14 }}"
  data-maptype="{{ settings.maptype | default: 'roadmap' }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    Only emitted when the card (and therefore the `<select>`) is absent — the parent has already
    resolved the query down its three tiers and escaped it, so it goes out verbatim. JS reads it only
    when there are no options, which is exactly this case.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if fallback_query != blank %}
    data-fallback-query="{{ fallback_query }}"
    data-fallback-title="{{ fallback_title }}"
  {% endif -%}
  {%- if shopify_attributes %}
    {{ shopify_attributes -}}
  {% endif %}
>
  {%- if render_card -%}
    <div class="maps__card" style="{{ card_style }}">
      <div class="maps__card-inner">
        <div class="maps__select select">
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="maps-select-{{ block_id }}">
            {{- 'blocks.maps.select_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <select
            id="maps-select-{{ block_id }}"
            class="maps__select-input form-control"
            ref="select"
            on:change="/handleSelect"
          >
            {{ options_html }}
          </select>
        </div>
        {{ panels_html }}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The placeholder is the NO-KEY surface ONLY — it is server-rendered when `api_key` is blank and
    never otherwise. It is deliberately NOT the pre-load surface: lifestyle artwork flashing while a
    map loads reads as "this block is an image", which is wrong on first view-entry and wrong again on
    every branch switch. Before the map arrives the box is simply empty at its configured height
    (`min-height` on `__map`), so there is still no layout shift. It uses Shopify's built-in
    `lifestyle-1` artwork — the theme's standard media placeholder (`_hero-banner-media`,
    `_image-compare-side`, `video-markup`) — with the muted `.placeholder` treatment.

    Loading is a SCRIM + the spinner, both `inset: 0` inside a box that already holds its height ⇒ no
    geometry change, CLS 0. The scrim is a translucent wash from the scheme background role, the
    spinner is the theme's own `loading-spinner` (absolutely positioned like every other overlay use
    of it, e.g. `cart-gift-wrapping`). Both are revealed by the `is-loading` STATE class on the root
    (state classes are the documented exception to the JS DOM contract, so `check-js-contract` stays
    green) and hidden again on the iframe's `load`. Both sit at `z-index: 1`, above the injected
    iframe (positioned but `z-index: auto`); the spinner is later in the DOM so it paints over the
    scrim.

    Placeholder and scrim are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE BY CONSTRUCTION: with a blank `api_key`
    `<maps-component>` returns before observing, no iframe is ever created and `is-loading` can never
    be set — so the no-key state shows the placeholder with no scrim and no spinner, and every
    loading state has no placeholder underneath it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="maps__map border-style" ref="map">
    {%- if has_api_key == false -%}
      <div class="maps__placeholder">
        {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'maps__placeholder-svg placeholder' }}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="maps__scrim"></div>
    {%- render 'loading-spinner', class: 'maps__spinner' -%}
  </div>

  {%- if show_onboarding -%}
    <p class="maps__onboarding paragraph">{{ 'blocks.maps.no_locations' | t }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</maps-component>
